# XSH tcsetpgrp()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# Same arrangement as tcgetpgrp(): a session of its own with a pseudo-terminal
# (XSI) as controlling terminal, a background caller that is not orphaned
# (child of the session leader in its own process group) where a signal is
# the point, and the session leader itself (whose group is orphaned, its
# parent being outside the session) where EIO is the point. Set-up calls that
# would be ambiguous for a caller in an orphaned foreground group are made
# with SIGTTOU ignored, which the page excludes from EIO. Bounded by
# alarm(); every process is reaped.
#
# "when BASE|XSI": the requirements are Base; XSI is named only so that the
# driver builds these tests with the XSI feature macro (the pseudo-terminal
# set-up needs it). They run wherever they build, and a set-up that is not
# available is UNRESOLVED.

assertion  XSH.tcsetpgrp.001
anchor     functions/tcsetpgrp.html#ERRORS/EBADF
class      required
since      1988
says       tcsetpgrp(-1, getpgrp()) and tcsetpgrp() of a closed descriptor
           return -1 with EBADF; ENOTTY is also accepted when the process
           has no controlling terminal that the ctermid() pathname opens
           (both errors then apply, XSH 2.3).
test       t/001-ebadf.c

assertion  XSH.tcsetpgrp.002
anchor     functions/tcsetpgrp.html#ERRORS/ENOTTY
class      required
since      1988
says       tcsetpgrp(fd, getpgrp()) on descriptors for a regular file,
           both ends of a pipe and /dev/null returns -1 with ENOTTY.
test       t/002-enotty-file.c

assertion  XSH.tcsetpgrp.003
anchor     functions/tcsetpgrp.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/tcsetpgrp.html#RETURN VALUE
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap11.html#11.1.2
class      conditional
when       BASE|XSI
since      1988
says       A process in the foreground group of its controlling terminal
           (a group that is not orphaned) calls tcsetpgrp() with the
           session leader's group; it returns 0 and tcgetpgrp() then
           returns that group.
note       XSI only for the pseudo-terminal set-up (posix_openpt() and its
           companions are XSI); the requirement itself is Base.
timeout    40
test       t/003-foreground-sets.c

assertion  XSH.tcsetpgrp.004
anchor     functions/tcsetpgrp.html#DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       BASE|XSI
since      1988
says       A process in a background group that is ignoring SIGTTOU calls
           tcsetpgrp() with its own group: it returns 0, is not stopped,
           and tcgetpgrp() then returns its group.
note       XSI only for the pseudo-terminal set-up (posix_openpt() and its
           companions are XSI); the requirement itself is Base.
timeout    40
test       t/004-bg-ignoring.c

assertion  XSH.tcsetpgrp.005
anchor     functions/tcsetpgrp.html#DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       BASE|XSI
since      1988
says       A process in a background group whose calling thread blocks
           SIGTTOU calls tcsetpgrp() with its own group: it returns 0 and
           SIGTTOU is not pending afterwards.
note       XSI only for the pseudo-terminal set-up (posix_openpt() and its
           companions are XSI); the requirement itself is Base.
timeout    40
test       t/005-bg-blocking.c

assertion  XSH.tcsetpgrp.006
anchor     functions/tcsetpgrp.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap11.html#11.1.4
class      conditional
when       BASE|XSI
since      1988
says       A process in a background group (not orphaned) that catches
           SIGTTOU calls tcsetpgrp() on its controlling terminal: the
           handler runs (the signal was sent to its group).
note       XSI only for the pseudo-terminal set-up (posix_openpt() and its
           companions are XSI); the requirement itself is Base. The
           handler then ignores SIGTTOU so that a restarted call
           completes; the call's own result is not examined.
timeout    40
test       t/006-bg-signal.c

assertion  XSH.tcsetpgrp.007
anchor     functions/tcsetpgrp.html#ERRORS/EIO
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap11.html#11.1.4
class      conditional
when       BASE|XSI
since      1988
says       A session leader whose process group is orphaned and in the
           background, neither ignoring nor blocking SIGTTOU, gets -1 with
           EIO from tcsetpgrp(), and its SIGTTOU handler does not run.
note       XSI only for the pseudo-terminal set-up (posix_openpt() and its
           companions are XSI); the requirement itself is Base. The caller
           is in the background, which every reading of the EIO condition
           covers (see the note on Q-82).
timeout    40
test       t/007-orphan-eio.c

assertion  XSH.tcsetpgrp.008
anchor     functions/tcsetpgrp.html#ERRORS/ENOTTY
class      conditional
when       BASE|XSI
since      1988
says       In a process with no controlling terminal, tcsetpgrp() on a
           pseudo-terminal subsidiary descriptor (opened with O_NOCTTY)
           returns -1 with ENOTTY.
note       XSI only for the pseudo-terminal set-up (posix_openpt() and its
           companions are XSI); the requirement itself is Base.
timeout    40
test       t/008-enotty-no-ctty.c

assertion  XSH.tcsetpgrp.009
anchor     functions/tcsetpgrp.html#ERRORS/ENOTTY
class      conditional
when       BASE|XSI
since      1988
says       In a process whose controlling terminal is one pseudo-terminal,
           tcsetpgrp() on the subsidiary descriptor of a different pseudo-
           terminal returns -1 with ENOTTY.
note       XSI only for the pseudo-terminal set-up (posix_openpt() and its
           companions are XSI); the requirement itself is Base.
timeout    40
test       t/009-enotty-other-tty.c

assertion  XSH.tcsetpgrp.010
anchor     functions/tcsetpgrp.html#ERRORS/EPERM
anchor     functions/tcsetpgrp.html#ERRORS/EINVAL
class      conditional
when       BASE|XSI
since      1988
says       tcsetpgrp() on the controlling terminal with the ID of a
           process group of another session (the test harness's) returns
           -1 with EPERM, or with EINVAL if the implementation does not
           support that value; the caller is ignoring SIGTTOU so that EIO
           cannot apply.
note       XSI only for the pseudo-terminal set-up (posix_openpt() and its
           companions are XSI); the requirement itself is Base.
timeout    40
test       t/010-eperm-other-session.c
